                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>In his inaugural address, delivered on November 8, 1953, President Figueres stated that the Costa Rican Government
                    planned to review its relations with the United Fruit Company. He also proposed
                    the renegotiation of the Company’s contract, which had been signed in 1948 and
                    was not scheduled to expire until 1988. The text of President Figueres’ address was transmitted to the
                    Department of State under cover of despatch 363, from San José, dated November
                    12, 1953, not printed (718.11/11–1253).</p>
            </div>
        </body>
